# RFC 9173 Appendix A.4, "Example 4 - Security Blocks with Full Scope".
# Copied from https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9173.txt (fetched 2026-10-24).
# Format: "name:" then hex on the following indented lines; '#' starts a comment.
# Scalars (in bpsec9173_test.go):
#   BIB: SHA variant HMAC 384/384 (6), scope 0x07, source ipn:2.1, target [1],
#        block number 3, flags 0, no CRC.
#   BCB: AES variant A256GCM (3), scope 0x07, source ipn:2.1, targets [3, 1],
#        block number 2, flags 1, no CRC; no wrapped key.
# NOTE: both BCB targets use one key and one IV; errata 7002 says this breaks
# §4.3.1 and that a BCB with an IV parameter should have one target.
# The primary and payload blocks are those of A.1 (A.4.1.1, A.4.1.2).

